Package: HDLCP
Type: Package
Title: Upper L-Statistics for High-Dimensional Change-Point Inference
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(person("Guowei", "Yan", role = "aut"),
    person("Dan", "Zhuang", role = "aut"),
    person("Long", "Feng", email = "flnankai@nankai.edu.cn", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Tests and localizes a single high-dimensional mean change using
    upper L-statistics, analytic finite-sample calibrations, Cauchy combinations,
    and minimum-component-p localization. Implements the v37 manuscript and
    provides seeded parallel Monte Carlo experiments for every simulation design,
    competitor interfaces, and the SECOM application.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: Rcpp, stats, utils, graphics, grDevices, parallel
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Suggests: DMS, CVXR (>= 1.9.0), testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Remotes: ghwang-nk/DMS
URL: https://github.com/flnankai/HDLCP
BugReports: https://github.com/flnankai/HDLCP/issues
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: C++17
